☀️ IN THE SUNSHINE – DAY 3☀️

Not all sunshine comes with sand and sunsets… sometimes it comes with theme music and a championship belt. 🏆

Today we feature Rtn Barrack Odero, President of https://t.me/rotaryclubofsyokimau and his moment in the sunshine? Watching WWE wrestling.

Yes. The suplexes. The dramatic entrances. The “it’s-not-scripted-it’s-strategic” debates. 😌

Because sometimes joy is switching off, picking your favourite wrestler, and fully committing to the storyline.

As we count down to the Eastern Region Sunshine Rally on 28th March☀️ **IN THE SUNSHINE – DAY 3** ☀️

Not all sunshine comes with sand and sunsets… sometimes it comes with theme music and a championship belt. 🏆

Today we feature **Rtn Barrack Odirro**, President of RC Syokimau — and his moment in the sunshine? Watching WWE wrestling.

Yes. The suplexes. The dramatic entrances. The “it’s-not-scripted-it’s-strategic” debates. 😌

Because sometimes joy is switching off, picking your favourite wrestler, and fully committing to the storyline like it’s a board resolution.

As we count down to the Eastern Region Sunshine Rally on 28th March 2026, we’re celebrating the moments that make us light up, big or small, as we prepare to create a day full of light, laughter, and belonging for children living with disabilities. 💛

Your moment in the sunshine doesn’t have to be serious.
It just has to be yours.

And don’t worry… we’re still scouting. You might be next. 👀☀️

#inthesunshine #easternregionsunshinerally #serviceaboveself 
