Yesterday, in commemoration of Water, Sanitation and Hygiene Month, we successfully carried out a project at Nkaimurunya Comprehensive School, marking the launch of a strategic partnership between Rotary District 9212, Pwani Oil Products Limited, Detrex, and Davis & Shirtliff.

The initiative was officially flagged off by PDG Leonard Ithau and attended by DGE District 9216, district leadership, Rotary and Rotaract clubs, alongside our partners.

A key focus of the engagement was hygiene education, with students taken through the importance of hand washing and practical demonstrations on proper techniques. These foundational habits are critical in promoting long term health outcomes within our communities.

Sincere thanks to all partners and participants who contributed to the success of this impactful day. 

